    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lineup today leans heavily on high-floor production against vulnerable pitching rotations, headlined by **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, who carries an elite 82.08 efficiency score. Despite facing Carlos Rod\u00f3n, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**\u2019s projection is buoyed by a strong 0.376 xwOBA and a favorable slot in the #2 hole, which maximizes his opportunities to drive in runs. Both **Nolan Schanuel** (64.30) and **Josh Lowe** (64.95) are our most reliable secondary options; they benefit significantly from facing Luis Severino, whose 4.60 xERA provides a soft landing for our hitters. While **Josh Lowe** is projected lower in the order, his dynamic platoon edge against the right-handed Severino makes him a high-upside play that mimics the production of our top-tier starters.\n\nThe most intriguing tactical decision today centers on the lower half of the lineup, specifically the contrast between **Dominic Smith** and **Nasim Nunez**. While **Nasim Nunez** is a vital asset for our SB-focused strategy, his efficiency score of 51.41 is hampered by a matchup against the veteran Peterson and a bottom-of-the-order penalty. **Dominic Smith** (53.57) edges him out due to a more favorable spot in the order and a +9% boost stemming from his platoon advantage against Sandy Alcantara. Meanwhile, we remain in a holding pattern with **Liam Hicks** (47.38); he is our most volatile start, as his score is heavily dependent on confirmation of the #8 spot. We are carefully monitoring the weather and confirmed lineups, particularly with **Liam Hicks**, **Nolan Schanuel**, **Josh Lowe**, **Dominic Smith**, and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** currently listed as \"Lineup Pending.\" We are intentionally sitting **Kyle Tucker**, **Gunnar Henderson**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, and **Andy Pages** to navigate the schedule gaps and injury status, ensuring we don't burn game caps on players unavailable or sidelined.",
